[24.343416, "o", "Help on class StdOutSink in module bytewax.connectors.stdio:\r\n\r\nclass StdOutSink(bytewax.outputs.DynamicSink)\r\n |  Write each output item to stdout on that worker.\r\n |\r\n |  Items consumed from the dataflow must look like a string. Use a\r\n |  proceeding map step to do custom formatting.\r\n |\r\n |  Workers are the unit of parallelism.\r\n |\r\n |  Can support at-least-once processing. Messages from the resume\r\n |  epoch will be duplicated right after resume.\r\n |\r\n |  Method resolution order:\r\n |      StdOutSink\r\n |      bytewax.outputs.DynamicSink\r\n |      bytewax.outputs.Sink\r\n |      abc.ABC\r\n |      typing.Generic\r\n |      builtins.object\r\n |\r\n |  Methods defined here:\r\n |\r\n |  build(self, _step_id: str, _worker_index: int, _worker_count: int) -> bytewax.connectors.stdio._PrintSinkPartition\r\n |      Build an output partition for a worker.\r\n |\r\n |      Will be called once on each worker.\r\n |\r\n |      :arg step_id: The step_id of the output operator.\r\n |\r\n"]
